#version 450
//! `out[i] = weights[i]`, a learned tensor copied into the activation arena.
//!
//! # Why an op exists for a copy
//!
//! Every other op reads its weights straight out of binding 1, so nothing needed this until
//! Supertonic's text encoder: its style attention's **keys** are
//! `tanh(W_key . style_key + b_key)`, and `style_key` is a learned `[50, 256]` table. All three
//! are constants, so the whole expression folds to one tensor at conversion time - but
//! `attn_scores.comp` contracts two *arena* tensors, and there was no way to get a weight
//! there.
//!
//! The alternatives were worse. Keeping the fold out and running `W_key` as a convolution needs
//! `style_key` in the arena anyway, so it would have to become a plan input - a model constant
//! travelling with the per-voice data. And `Kind::Embed` over a ramp of ids would do this
//! today, which is a copy dressed as a lookup.
//!
//! # It is not free, and that is fine
//!
//! One dispatch and one write per element. The tensors this is for are small (25 KB for the
//! text encoder's) and it runs once per plan, against 9M parameters of convolution.

#include "common.glsl"

void main() {
    uint index = global_index();
    if (index >= p.count) {
        return;
    }
    arena[p.out_at + index] = weights[p.weight + index];
}
